{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/init(realm:asURI:pat:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/pat","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/realm"],"title":"Instance Properties"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13UmaChallengerV","title":"UmaChallenger"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A configured "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WWW-Authenticate: UMA"},{"type":"text","text":" challenge emitter (CONTRACT.md §20.3, emit half)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UmaChallenger"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hand one to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamGuards\/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and a denial stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"being a bare 403: the guard mints a fresh permission ticket for the pair the caller lacked and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches it to the thrown ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", so the framework adapter can return it as a header and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a UMA-aware client knows where to go for authority instead of only being told “no”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in, and deliberately so."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Emitting a challenge means minting a credential — a wire call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the Protection API, and a live ticket, produced on a path the caller did not explicitly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request. A guard that did that on every denial by default would turn each unauthorized request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into a Protection API call, which is a denial-of-service amplifier pointed at your own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authorization server. So it happens only where an application asked for it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Failure is not escalation.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" If minting fails — the PAT expired, the Protection API is down,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the resource declares none of the requested scopes — the denial still surfaces as an ordinary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","isActive":true},{"text":" without a challenge. A caller who was going to be refused is refused either way;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"letting a Protection API outage turn a deny into a 503 would hand the outage a second","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consequence, and letting it turn into an allow would be a security bug.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger"},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamClient/umaDiscover()":{"title":"umaDiscover()","abstract":[{"code":"GET \/.well-known\/uma2-configuration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (§20.1) — fetch the UMA discovery document.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/umadiscover()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"umaDiscover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Uma2Configuration","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK17Uma2ConfigurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/umaDiscover()"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/asURI":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger\/asuri","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"asURI","abstract":[{"text":"The authorization server the caller should redeem the ticket at — normally this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deployment’s issuer, read from ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/umaDiscover()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" rather than concatenated by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hand, for the same reason §12.3 rule 6 gives.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"asURI","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI"},"doc://AxiamSDK/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AuthzError":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/authzerror","title":"AuthzError","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AuthzError","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AuthzError","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Authorization failure (§2). Carries a ","type":"text"},{"code":"message","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and, when the server provided them,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the denied ","type":"text"},{"code":"action","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"resourceID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/realm":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger\/realm","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The protection realm named in the header.","type":"text"}],"title":"realm","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/realm","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"realm","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","title":"AxiamSDK","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamGuards/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)":{"abstract":[{"code":"require_access(action, resource[, scope])","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (§11): the ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"authenticated caller"}]},{"text":" must pass","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an AXIAM authorization check. ","type":"text"},{"code":"subject_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the end user’s id (§11.2 rule 2), not the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"application’s service-account session."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamGuards\/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"requireAccess"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"resource"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"scope"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"umaChallenge"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK13UmaChallengerV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UmaChallenger"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A12GuardHandlera","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AxiamGuardHandler"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamguards\/requireaccess(_:resource:scope:umachallenge:)"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/init(realm:asURI:pat:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/init(realm:asURI:pat:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger\/init(realm:asuri:pat:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"